# Reverse Proxy Configuration in Production

1. Identify and configure a reverse proxy (e.g., Nginx, Caddy, ALB, Cloudflare) to terminate TLS and route traffic.
2. Ensure the proxy forces HTTPS for all incoming connections.
3. Configure the reverse proxy to load balance requests across your app servers.
4. Use the proxy to hide internal server addresses from clients.
5. Implement additional cross-cutting concerns like rate limiting, authentication gates, caching, compression, access logs, and WAF rules using the reverse proxy.
